**Reproduced** on `6cc1281`: `strace -e trace=openat ./target/debug/rb test` opens `tests/redblue_test.rs`; and a probe `tests/zz_probe_test.rs` containing a `// test`/`// end` block makes `rb test` print `Failed: 1`, exit 1 — Rust source reported as a Redblue failure. (Note: the checked-in `.rs` files have no column-0 marker line, so the failure is latent on `main`, not constant. Recorded honestly in REPORT.md; the DoD "no `.rs` is ever read" was objectively unmet.)

**Fix** (28 added / 16 removed, 2 files):
- `src/testing/mod.rs:57` — `find_test_files` collects `.rb` only; recursion split into `collect_test_files` and result sorted (`read_dir` order is nondeterministic). `run_all_tests`' redundant `_test.rs || .rb` filter deleted.
- `src/testing/harness.rs:58` — `TestHarness::run_file` refuses non-`.rb` with `Error::Io`, so `rb test foo.rs` is rejected before any read.

**Tests**: 9 new `#[test]` in `src/testing/mod.rs::discovery_tests`, fixtures under `$CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR`. Watched 6 fail for the right reason before the fix; 4 named `edge_*`; two assert a failure is produced (`run_file_rejects_a_rust_source`, `a_failing_expect_is_still_reported_as_a_failure` — the anti-muting guard).

**Gates**: fmt pass · clippy `-D warnings` pass · `cargo test --all-targets` 55 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored · **`./rbops/verify.sh phase-002` NOT RUN — `rbops/` does not exist in this checkout**, so I am not claiming it passed. Substitute proofs: all 6 `examples/*.rb` exit 0, `rb test` → `Failed: 0`/exit 0, and `strace` shows only the 3 `.rb` files opened.

`phases/phase-002/REPORT.md` and `FINDINGS.md` written (7 follow-ups filed, none silently fixed).

